Hook payment processing to steal card details

Bypass promo code validation for unlimited discounts

Manipulate order totals before submission

Intercept push notifications to steal order details

6. Deep Link Security Vulnerabilities (MEDIUM-HIGH RISK)
Deep Link Injection Attacks​

Deep links allow external apps/websites to open your app with parameters. Improperly validated deep links enable attackers to bypass authentication, access unauthorized features, or inject malicious data.

Vulnerable Deep Link Handling:​

dart
// VULNERABLE - No validation
class DeepLinkHandler {
  static void handleLink(String deepLink) {
    final uri = Uri.parse(deepLink);
    
    // DANGEROUS: Direct use of parameters
    if (uri.path == '/order') {
      final orderId = uri.queryParameters['id']; // No validation!
      navigateToOrder(orderId); // Attacker can access any order
    }
    
    if (uri.path == '/payment') {
      final amount = uri.queryParameters['amount']; // Price manipulation!
      processPayment(amount);
    }
    
    if (uri.path == '/webview') {
      final url = uri.queryParameters['url']; // XSS vulnerability!
      loadWebView(url); // Can load malicious sites
    }
  }
}
Secure Deep Link Implementation:​

dart
class SecureDeepLinkHandler {
  static const allowedHosts = ['yourapp.com', 'app.yourapp.com'];
  static const allowedSchemes = ['https', 'yourapp'];
  static final orderIdPattern = RegExp(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{20,30}$');
  static final userIdPattern = RegExp(r'^[0-9]{6,12}$');
  
  static Future<void> handleDeepLink(String deepLink) async {
    try {
      final uri = Uri.parse(deepLink);
      
      // 1. Validate scheme
      if (!allowedSchemes.contains(uri.scheme)) {
        throw SecurityException('Invalid scheme: ${uri.scheme}');
      }
      
      // 2. Validate host (for HTTPS deep links)
      if (uri.scheme == 'https' && !allowedHosts.contains(uri.host)) {
        throw SecurityException('Invalid host: ${uri.host}');
      }
      
      // 3. Route with parameter validation
      switch (uri.path) {
        case '/order':
          await _handleOrderLink(uri);
          break;
        case '/restaurant':
          await _handleRestaurantLink(uri);
          break;
        case '/promo':
          await _handlePromoLink(uri);
          break;
        default:
          // Unknown path - navigate to safe default
          await _navigateToHome();
      }
    } catch (e) {
      // Log security violation
      await _logSecurityEvent('deep_link_violation', deepLink);
      await _navigateToHome(); // Safe fallback
    }
  }
  
  static Future<void> _handleOrderLink(Uri uri) async {
    final orderId = uri.queryParameters['id'];
    
    // Validate format
    if (orderId == null || !orderIdPattern.hasMatch(orderId)) {
      throw SecurityException('Invalid order ID format');
    }
    
    // Verify user has access to this order
    final hasAccess = await OrderService.verifyUserAccess(orderId);
    if (!hasAccess) {
      throw SecurityException('Unauthorized order access attempt');
    }
    
    navigateToOrder(orderId);
  }
  
  static Future<void> _handlePromoLink(Uri uri) async {
    final promoCode = uri.queryParameters['code'];
    
    // Never trust client-side promo validation
    // Always verify with backend
    final isValid = await PromoService.validateCode(promoCode);
    if (!isValid) {
      showError('Invalid promo code');
      return;
    }
    
    applyPromoCode(promoCode);
  }
}
Deep Link Security Rules:​

Validate scheme (only allow your custom scheme + HTTPS)

Whitelist allowed hosts for HTTPS links

Validate parameter formats with regex patterns

Never use deep link parameters directly in SQL, file paths, or WebViews

Verify user authorization before accessing resources via deep link

Log all deep link accesses for fraud detection​

Food Delivery Deep Link Attacks:

yourapp://order?id=OTHER_USER_ORDER → IDOR vulnerability

yourapp://payment?amount=0.01 → Price manipulation

yourapp://driver?fake_location=true → GPS spoofing

yourapp://promo?code=EXPIRED123 → Discount fraud

https://yourapp.com/reset-password?token=STOLEN → Account takeover

7. WebView Security (MEDIUM-HIGH RISK)
XSS and Code Injection via WebView​

WebViews loading untrusted content are major attack vectors. JavaScript enabled in WebViews can access app data if not properly isolated.

Secure WebView Configuration:​

dart
import 'package:webview_flutter/webview_flutter.dart';

class SecureWebViewController {
  late final WebViewController controller;
  
  void initWebView() {
    controller = WebViewController()
      // 1. Disable JavaScript unless absolutely necessary
      ..setJavaScriptMode(JavaScriptMode.disabled)
      
      // 2. Whitelist allowed domains
      ..setNavigationDelegate(
        NavigationDelegate(
          onNavigationRequest: (request) {
            final uri = Uri.parse(request.url);
            
            // Only allow specific trusted domains
            if (uri.host == 'menu.yourrestaurant.com' ||
                uri.host == 'help.yourapp.com') {
              return NavigationDecision.navigate;
            }
            
            // Block all other domains
            return NavigationDecision.prevent;
          },
        ),
      )
      
      // 3. Clear cache on close
      ..clearCache()
      ..clearLocalStorage();
  }
  
  // If JavaScript MUST be enabled
  void initWebViewWithJS() {
    controller = WebViewController()
      ..setJavaScriptMode(JavaScriptMode.unrestricted) // Only if required
      
      // 4. Sanitize any data passed to WebView
      ..loadHtmlString(_sanitizeHtml(dynamicContent))
      
      // 5. NEVER use addJavaScriptChannel with sensitive data
      // Attackers can call these channels from injected JS
      ..addJavaScriptChannel(
        'messageHandler',
        onMessageReceived: (message) {
          // Validate all messages from WebView
          if (_isValidMessage(message.message)) {
            handleMessage(message.message);
          }
        },
      );
  }
  
  static String _sanitizeHtml(String html) {
    // Remove <script> tags, event handlers, etc.
    return html
        .replaceAll(RegExp(r'<script[^>]*>.*?</script>', dotAll: true), '')
        .replaceAll(RegExp(r'on\w+\s*='), ''); // Remove onclick, onerror, etc.
  }
}
WebView Security Checklist:​

Disable JavaScript unless absolutely required

Whitelist allowed domains in NavigationDelegate

Never load user-provided URLs without validation

Sanitize any HTML content before loading

Clear WebView cache and cookies on logout/close

Never expose sensitive app functions via JavaScriptChannel

Validate all messages from WebView JavaScript​

Food Delivery WebView Risks:

Restaurant menu pages loading malicious JavaScript

Help center articles with XSS vulnerabilities

Third-party payment pages stealing card details

Promotional content injecting tracking scripts

8. Permission Over-Requesting & Privacy (MEDIUM RISK)
Minimal Permission Principle​

Requesting unnecessary permissions raises privacy concerns and increases app rejection risk. Elite teams request only essential permissions with clear justifications.

Permission Best Practices:​

dart
import 'package:permission_handler/permission_handler.dart';

class PermissionManager {
  // Request permissions with user explanation FIRST
  static Future<bool> requestLocationPermission() async {
    // 1. Show custom dialog explaining WHY
    final userAgreed = await _showPermissionRationale(
      'Location Access',
      'We need your location to show nearby restaurants and provide accurate delivery.',
    );
    
    if (!userAgreed) return false;
    
    // 2. Request OS permission
    final status = await Permission.locationWhenInUse.request();
    
    // 3. Handle all possible states
    if (status.isGranted) {
      return true;
    } else if (status.isDenied) {
      _showPermissionDenied();
      return false;
    } else if (status.isPermanentlyDenied) {
      // User must enable in settings
      await openAppSettings();
      return false;
    }
    
    return false;
  }
  
  // Request camera only when needed (order photo upload)
  static Future<bool> requestCameraPermission() async {
    // Don't request at app startup - only when user wants to upload photo
    final status = await Permission.camera.request();
    return status.isGranted;
  }
  
  // NEVER request unnecessary permissions
  static Future<void> checkUnnecessaryPermissions() async {
    // ❌ DON'T request these for food delivery app:
    // - READ_CONTACTS (no need for contact list)
    // - RECORD_AUDIO (unless voice ordering feature)
    // - READ_SMS (unless OTP auto-fill, use SMS Retriever API instead)
    // - ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION (use ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION for restaurant search)
  }
}
