=== FOOD DELIVERY SPECIFIC CHECKS ===
1. Customer addresses encrypted in secure storage, not SharedPreferences
2. Driver location not tracked when off-duty
3. Payment card data NEVER stored locally (use tokenization)
4. Restaurant API keys proxied through backend
5. Promo code validation always server-side
6. Order total calculation on backend (prevent client-side manipulation)
7. GPS location validated server-side (detect spoofing)
8. Push notification tokens rotated on device change

For each risk found:
- Severity: CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW
- Platform: iOS / Android / Both
- Vulnerable Code: Show exact line
- Secure Code: Provide fixed implementation
- Attack Scenario: Explain exploitation in food delivery context
- Impact: Data breach / Financial loss / Service disruption

Focus on risks that cause:
- Customer data theft (addresses, phone numbers, order history)
- Payment fraud (card details, unauthorized charges)
- Account takeover (token theft, session hijacking)
- Business logic bypass (pricing manipulation, promo fraud)
- GPS spoofing (fake driver location, delivery fraud)

